rows=[{'id':f'atelier-{i+1:02}-{k}','key':k,'style':sty,'title':title,'concept':concept,'theme':theme,'start':i*4,'duration':4,'source':f'compositions/{i+1:02}-{k}.html'} for i,(k,sty,title,concept,theme) in enumerate(scenes)]
(P/'overlay-timeline.json').write_text(json.dumps({'version':1,'scenes':rows},indent=2))
(P/'metadata.json').write_text(json.dumps({'slug':'style-atelier','title':'ATELIER / Richer by Design','duration':64,'width':1920,'height':1080,'fps':30,'scope':'motion-asset-pack'},indent=2))
(P/'sources.json').write_text(json.dumps({'version':1,'sources':[]},indent=2))
(P/'creative-brief.md').write_text('# ATELIER / Richer by Design\n\nUser scope: enrich all seven style-library families plus FORM / FREQUENCY assets. Standalone asset collection and locally rendered demonstration; no Dena narration or publish action. 112 original layered SVGs, 16 four-second scenes, 64 seconds, 1920×1080, 30 fps.\n\nConcept: a motion atelier turns an idea into type, relation, sketch, paper, document, collage, layered world and sculptural material.\n')
(P/'design.md').write_text('# Atelier design\n\nInk #171918, paper #F1EEE5, cobalt #244BFF, vermilion #FA593D, acid #D9FC59, lilac #B6A3EF. Shared with FORM / FREQUENCY; varied family fields demonstrate range, rather than prescribing a mix of seven styles for one actual edit. Archivo Black for large display, Instrument Serif for expressive editorial copy, JetBrains Mono for edge furniture, Caveat for authored sketch labels. All local with OFL licenses.\n\n80 px title-safe border; heroes 900–1400 px wide, display 135–235 px, labels 26–34 px. Quiet label zones. Background texture, single strong hero, secondary live type, accent geometry, registration, chapter meter and fine rules.\n\nRhythm: slam / stretch / build / route / draw / close / unfold / launch / focus / connect / gather / paste / breathe / drift / sculpt / resolve. Two bars per scene at 120 BPM. Hard chapter cuts retain the last reading pose; entrances inherit directional energy. Paper, VOX and collage quantize every graphic pose to 15 steps/s. No paper blur or crossfades.\n')
(P/'storyboard.md').write_text('# Sixteen style studies\n\n'+''.join(f'{i+1:02}. {r["start"]}–{r["start"]+4}s — **{r["title"]}** ({r["style"]}) — {r["concept"]}\n\n' for i,r in enumerate(rows)))
(P/'visual-plan.md').write_text('# Visual plan\n\n## Style world\n\nAn asset-library demonstration, with two contrasting studies per family. Palette and typography: design.md. This collection demonstrates options; actual Dena edits choose at most three style types, semantically tied to the transcript.\n\n## Visual Decision Log\n\n'+''.join(f'- {r["id"]}: purpose demonstrate {r["style"]}; original designed SVGs with independent named parts; {r["concept"]} No proof captures or invented client results.\n' for r in rows)+'\n## Assembly\n\nTrack 1: sequential full-frame scene mounts. Track 20: original mastered music + SFX. Sixteen self-contained templates; SVG parts inline at setup, unique ids per instance; local SK.clip registers one deterministic paused timeline per study. Mix-media is a template study with a labelled speaker slot; production substitutes the exact-window real matte.\n\n## Review result\n\nUser explicitly chose all seven styles plus the showreel. Asset-production scope authorizes local source generation, assembly and rendering. Publish remains separate.\n')
(P/'.hyperframes/expanded-prompt.md').write_text('# ATELIER — Expanded production breakdown\n\nDesign spec: design.md. Fonts: Archivo Black, Instrument Serif, JetBrains Mono, Caveat. Palette #171918 / #F1EEE5 / #244BFF / #FA593D / #D9FC59 / #B6A3EF.\n\nRhythm: slam-stretch-build-route-draw-close-unfold-launch-focus-connect-gather-paste-breathe-drift-sculpt-resolve.\n\n'+''.join(f'## {i+1:02} — {r["title"]}\n\nConcept: {r["concept"]}\nMood: working design atelier; tactile construction and precise hierarchy.\nBG: full-bleed {r["theme"]} field, sparse structural grid, subtle paper/print material, moving chapter meter.\nMG: independent {r["style"]} hero parts; live display copy reveals on successive half-beats; focus lands by local 2.8s and holds.\nFG: 80px safe edge labels, registration crosses, source/illustration note, short accent rule.\nChoreography: {r["concept"]} Secondary motifs shift once after landing, then settle.\nTransition out: hard chapter cut at {r["start"]+4}s; direction inherited by the next study. SFX marks each major material gesture, quieter sketch/document gestures and deeper sculptural attacks.\n\n' for i,r in enumerate(rows))+'Negative direction: no fake Dena, real outlet, metric, remote dependency, wall-clock motion, endless decorative bouncing, or generic palette variants.\n')

